  "regulatory_and_legal_discussion": {
    "disparate_treatment_vs_disparate_impact": "Post-processing via ThresholdOptimizer achieves the lowest Demographic Parity and Equalized Odds gaps, but it requires passing the applicant's protected attribute (SEX or AGE_GROUP) at prediction time to apply group-specific cutoffs. Under fair-lending frameworks such as the US Equal Credit Opportunity Act (ECOA) and EU non-discrimination directives, explicitly applying different credit score cutoffs based on sex or age constitutes Disparate Treatment, which is generally prohibited even when motivated by reducing Disparate Impact. Therefore, in regulated lending, Pre-processing (Sample Reweighing) and In-processing (ExponentiatedGradient) are strongly preferred because they do not use protected attributes at inference time."
  }
}